author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Budgets are measured against fixtures at declared scale tiers including at least one workspace of repository size or larger, and each budget records the tier it was measured at, so a ceiling can no longer be set on a micro-workspace and read as a product guarantee; The corpus covers the MCP tools/list handshake payload and the aggregate per-command help surface, sourced from the same measurement the gate uses, so both have ceilings that fail on growth; The gate consumes scripts/measure-agent-token-surface.mjs rather than duplicating measurement, and a single command reproduces every published figure; A coverage assertion fails when a command, MCP tool, or output format exists with no budget entry, so new surfaces cannot be added outside the corpus; The gate reports the delta against the recorded baseline, not only pass or fail, so a change that consumes headroom without breaching is visible in review; The current 31-tool handshake and 76-command help surface are recorded as the new baseline with their measurement method, superseding the stale pm-a22j 28-tool figure wherever it is cited"
parent: pm-u9d0
